{
  "answer": "You can configure CORS to allow requests from specific origins in FastAPI by using the `CORSMiddleware` and specifying the `allow_origins` argument. Here is an example of how to do this:\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n# Define allowed origins\nallowed_origins = [\"https://example.com\", \"https://www.example.com\"]\n\n# Configure CORSMiddleware\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=allowed_origins,\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"]\n)\n```\n\nThis configuration is supported by the documentation in [tutorial/cors-5].",
